Text:
fearlessMessage is a program that sends one Message to the 'single' manager, and prints the Answer of the 'single' manager on its standard output.

Grammar:
Message ::= "EditMetadata " Base16
Base16 ::= "Base16:" ([0-9A-F][0-9A-F])+
Greeting ::= Base16 "\n"
Answer ::= "Applied\n" | "Refused\n" Error
Error ::= ...

Well formedness:
in Base16: second component is a valid OS FS path when decoded
in Greeting: the Base16 encodes the 'manager path'

Story:
A event fearlessMessage is called with syntax   fearlessMessage "Message"
B action fearlessMessage$send(Message)

Story:
A event fearlessMessage is called with arguments that are not one Message
B action fearlessMessage prints details to standard error
C action fearlessMessage ends with exit code 1

Define fearlessMessage$send(Message):
A fact A process holds the lock of single_manager_at_Port.lock, in the folder at the 'manager path'
B action fearlessMessage tries to open a connection to Port on the loopback address
C fact Within 5 seconds, fearlessMessage reads a Greeting from the connection
D action fearlessMessage sends Message "\n" on the connection
E action fearlessMessage prints the text that fearlessMessage reads from the connection, as soon as fearlessMessage reads that text, until the connection ends
F action fearlessMessage ends

Define fearlessMessage$send(Message):
A fact A process holds the lock of single_manager_at_Port.lock, in the folder at the 'manager path'
B action fearlessMessage tries to open a connection to Port on the loopback address
C fact The connection does not open, or within 5 seconds fearlessMessage does not read a Greeting from the connection
D action fearlessMessage ends the connection, if the connection is open
E action fearlessMessage$send(Message)

Define fearlessMessage$send(Message):
A fact A process holds the lock of no_manager.lock, in the folder at the 'manager path'
B action fearlessMessage waits until A does not hold
C action fearlessMessage$send(Message)

Define fearlessMessage$send(Message):
A fact No process holds the lock of a LockFile in the folder at the 'manager path'
B action fearlessMessage runs fearlessManager
C action fearlessMessage waits until A does not hold, or until fearlessManager ends
D action fearlessMessage$send(Message)

Implementation notes:
A connection is TCP on the loopback address.
On a connection the text is UTF-8; fearlessMessage prints the text with the encoding of its standard output.
fearlessMessage finds whether a process holds the lock of a LockFile by trying to take that lock with FileChannel.tryLock; when fearlessMessage takes the lock, fearlessMessage releases the lock at once.
fearlessManager runs in a process of its own, independent of fearlessMessage: fearlessManager does not keep the standard output and the standard error of fearlessMessage.
The bytes of a Base16 path: on Windows the UTF-16 code units of the name, little endian (a name may contain an unpaired surrogate); elsewhere the bytes of the name as the file system stores them.
